# Experiment Workflow

When working on training, evaluation, inference, OPSD, checkpoints, datasets, or experiment scripts:

1. Before acting, read `experiments/ACTIVE.md`, `experiments/LESSONS.md`, and the active registry YAML.
2. Before launching a job, check for an existing process, owner, GPU allocation, job ID, and output directory.
3. Register the current owner/window purpose, resources, command, and job ID in `experiments/ACTIVE.md`.
4. Use one `experiment_id` for the same model setting; keep training and evaluation in the same registry file.
5. Record actual parameters and artifact paths rather than relying on script defaults.
6. On any failure, append an `issues` entry with symptom, evidence, root cause, solution, status, and prevention before retrying.
7. Preserve resolved issues. Move reusable prevention guidance into `experiments/LESSONS.md`.
8. Before handoff or completion, update `handoff`, `activity_log`, phase status, metrics, conclusion, and next action.
9. Never put secrets, model weights, datasets, caches, or full logs in `experiments/`.
10. Do not launch a duplicate job when shared state is unclear; inspect actual processes and artifacts first.
11. All training from 2026-09-10 onward must run in conda `sr_opsd` (LESSON-041). Do not launch SFT or MV-OPSD in `spatialstack-qwen35`, `vision-opd`, or system python + `~/.local`. Evaluation may still use another env when the registry records it. Override only with `ALLOW_NON_SROPSD=1` and an issues note.

